WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
An initial rule handles a bounded set of cases.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
A new case requires an exception and may conflict with another rule.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.867
Maintenance grows as conditions change; automating a rule does not solve all its exceptions.

4
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:29.217
A flexible curve can pass through all training points.

5
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:36.383
Held-out points test whether the fit preserves the pattern beyond the sample.

6
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:43.733
Low training error does not guarantee low error on new data.

7
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:52.150
Use loss L equals w minus three squared, starting at w equals zero.

8
00:00:52.150 --> 00:01:00.450
The gradient is minus six. A step size of zero point two moves w to one point two.

9
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:08.867
Loss falls from 9 to 3.24; the next step recomputes the gradient.

10
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:16.217
In XOR, the two opposite corners with one active input have label one.

11
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:23.067
No straight line separates those corners from the other two in the original plane.

12
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:30.417
A nonlinear transformation can distinguish the case with exactly one active input.

13
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:37.767
A network composes operations: x passes through two weights before producing an output.

14
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:44.617
The chain rule connects loss changes to each intermediate operation.

15
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:51.967
Backpropagation reuses those derivatives to update weights across layers.

16
00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:59.317
A trigram model conditions the next token on the previous two.

17
00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:07.233
Two sentences with the same ending receive the same short context despite different earlier topics.

18
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:14.900
Limited memory simplifies the model and removes dependencies outside the window.

